Achu Recipe

Ingredients:

2kg cocoyams

1 teaspoon limestone (kanwa) or food-grade achu spice, if available

Red palm oil

Fresh pepper to taste

Salt to taste

2 seasoning cubes

1kg beef or cow skin

Smoked fish (optional)

Water as needed

Preparation:

Wash the cocoyams thoroughly and place them in a pot. Add water and boil until they are completely soft.

Peel the cocoyams while still warm and pound them in a mortar until smooth. Add a little warm water if necessary and continue pounding until the achu becomes stretchy and lump-free.

Alternatively, use a strong blender or food processor, adding as little water as possible.

Wash the beef and cow skin. Put them in a pot with salt, seasoning cubes, and a little water. Cook until tender. Add smoked fish if desired.

To prepare the yellow soup, place a small amount of red palm oil in a bowl. Add a little warm water and a small quantity of food-grade limestone or achu spice, if using. Stir carefully until the mixture becomes smooth and yellow.

Add pepper, salt, and seasoning to taste. Add more warm water gradually until the soup reaches your preferred consistency.

Serve the smooth achu with the yellow soup, beef, cow skin, and smoked fish.
